# Goal
string description
# Frames to plan over (the unified image buffer, owned by hint_narrative and
# passed in the goal — this node keeps NO buffer of its own). Order is meaningful,
# oldest first: the LAST image is the current view the path is planned on; any
# earlier ones are recent past views given as continuity. Empty = no frame (the
# call aborts). Mirrors VisualReason.images so both VLM nodes reason over one buffer.
sensor_msgs/CompressedImage[] images
---
# Result
# Success/failure is the action's terminal status (SUCCEEDED vs ABORTED) — no
# redundant `success` bool. Any interpretable plan (even empty markers = turn-only)
# SUCCEEDS; only a call that could not run (no frame / timeout / API error /
# unparseable reply) ABORTS, with the reason in `message`.
string message
# Ordered ground path in normalized image space: point.x, point.y in
# [-1, 1] (center = 0; left/top = -1, right/bottom = +1); z unused. markers[0]
# is the first (nearest) waypoint, markers[-1] the last (farthest).
geometry_msgs/Point[] markers
# Signed in-place rotation to apply after following the path (degrees), measured
# from the heading the robot ends the path with. + = left (CCW), - = right (CW),
# 0 = none. Executed by the Nav2 Spin behavior. markers may be empty with a
# non-zero turn_degrees: a turn-only move (scan / re-orient without driving).
float64 turn_degrees
# Stamp of the current-view frame the path was planned on (images[-1].header.stamp).
# FollowVisualPath grounds the markers into odom using the pose at this stamp.
builtin_interfaces/Time stamp
---
# Feedback
string state
